ing-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"**Out-of-band console** (IPMI/iDRAC) — heavy Jobs can still wedge SSH if you skip Guard"},"747":{"id":"/getting-started-26","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Operator client (the machine that runs Ansible and `manage.sh`): Ansible ≥ 2.14, kubectl, helm, **bazelisk**"},"748":{"id":"/getting-started-27","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"One command installs and verifies everything (Homebrew, no sudo):"},"749":{"id":"/getting-started-28","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Same script, apt/dnf based:"},"750":{"id":"/getting-started-29","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Install WSL2 + Ubuntu once (PowerShell), then the same script inside WSL:"},"751":{"id":"/getting-started-30","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"`status` subcommand reports what is already present; see Shell reference for the full contract."},"752":{"id":"/getting-started-31","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Never proceed without inventory ping and OOB access. Do not start kimi / Mode B/C until `start-test` succeeds."},"753":{"id":"/getting-started-32","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"The declarative topology `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml` is the single source of truth for\n**all five configurations** — node names/IPs, fabric, switch port map, and which Spark is\nthe orchestrator. Edit it, then render:"},"754":{"id":"/getting-started-33","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Rendering produces the Ansible inventory (`ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`, gitignored),\nfabric group vars, per-node netplan, and per-node cloud-init user-data — all from the\ntopology file. Full model: Lab topology."},"755":{"id":"/getting-started-34","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: none`, one node with `role: orchestrator`. No high-speed cabling, local NCCL only."},"756":{"id":"/getting-started-35","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: pair`, two nodes with both `hs_ifs` (dual QSFP direct). `group_vars` `highspeed_*`\nis the **pair** NCCL reference."},"757":{"id":"/getting-started-36","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: ring`, three nodes, QSFP triangle. **Not** “2-node plus spark2 with pair env” —\ncabling and Job env: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"758":{"id":"/getting-started-37","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: switch` + `switch:` block (CRS804-4DDQ-hRM `port_map`, one entry per node; 5 nodes\nuse breakout lanes `sfpplus4a`/`sfpplus4b`). Do **not** paste 